{"scripts/test-gcal-webhooks.sh uses sed -i '' which is macOS-specific and fails with GNU sed on Linux": 0.9643719792366028, "CredentialActionsDropdown's deleteCache mutation never invalidates/refetches viewer.calendars.connectedCalendars, so the dropdown continues to show the old cacheUpdatedAt after a successful delete": 0.993299126625061, "apps/web's dev:cron script uses npx tsx but tsx is not declared in the workspace's dependencies, making the script non-reproducible and dependent on external network/tooling state": 0.8615404963493347, "deleteCacheHandler throws a plain Error when a credential is missing/unauthorized instead of a typed TRPCError with NOT_FOUND/UNAUTHORIZED code, preventing clients from distinguishing auth failures from server failures": 0.9156478643417358, "connectedCalendarsHandler directly instantiates CalendarCacheRepository bypassing the CalendarCache.init feature-flag gate, causing an extra DB query even when the calendar-cache feature is globally disabled": 0.9728068709373474, "GoogleCalendarService.fetchAvailabilityAndSetCache runs SelectedCalendarRepository.updateManyByCredentialId after refreshing cache, adding an extra database write on webhook-driven paths which can increase DB write load proportionally to webhook volume": 0.8103278875350952}